  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="sp-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h2">
    <div class="sp-faq-inner">
      <p class="sp-section-label">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="sp-section-h2" id="faq-h2">Natural Stone &amp; Limestone FAQ<br><em>Answered Honestly</em></h2>
      <div class="sp-faq-list" role="list">

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-1">
            What's the difference between natural stone, limestone, and manufactured stone?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-1" role="region">
            <p>Natural stone (fieldstone, bluestone, granite) is quarried in irregular shapes and finished on site. Limestone is a sedimentary stone that cuts cleanly and gives a refined, architectural look — especially popular on Chicago North Shore homes. Manufactured stone veneer is a concrete product that mimics stone appearance but doesn't have the same durability or authentic look. AMS installs natural stone and limestone only — not manufactured veneer.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-2">
            How do I know if my home can support limestone?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-2" role="region">
            <p>Limestone is heavy — full veneers require a proper ledger, flashing, and structural support. We assess structural capacity on every estimate visit before recommending a full limestone facade.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-3">
            Is limestone good for Chicago winters?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-3" role="region">
            <p>Yes — Indiana limestone in particular is quarried for Chicago's climate and has been used on North Shore homes for over a century. Proper waterproofing and sealing are essential. AMS seals every limestone installation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-4">
            How long does natural stone installation take?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-4" role="region">
            <p>Accent features (fireplaces, chimneys, entries) run 2–5 days. Partial facades take 1–2 weeks. Full exterior stone can run 3–6 weeks. Timeline depends heavily on stone selection and custom cutting.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-5">
            Can you match stone on an existing home?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-5" role="region">
            <p>Matching existing stone requires finding stone from the same or compatible quarry source. AMS has an established supplier network and will source samples for your approval before committing. Some stones are unavailable or have changed color in new quarry batches — we'll tell you upfront.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-6">
            Does natural stone need to be sealed?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-6" role="region">
            <p>Yes — in Chicago's climate, sealing is non-optional for limestone and most porous natural stones. AMS applies appropriate penetrating sealer after every installation and recommends resealing every 5–7 years.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-7">
            Do you do interior stone work?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-7" role="region">
            <p>Yes — fireplaces, feature walls, kitchen backsplashes, and interior accent features. Interior stone work follows the same standards as exterior, with appropriate substrate and adhesive systems.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sp-faq-item" role="listitem">
          <button class="sp-faq-q" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-a-8">
            How much does limestone installation cost?
            <svg class="sp-faq-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
          </button>
          <div class="sp-faq-a" id="faq-a-8" role="region">
            <p>Limestone installation in Chicagoland typically runs $25–$65 per square foot installed, depending on stone selection, custom cutting requirements, and substrate preparation. Free on-site estimates at 773-656-2107.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

